  "authored_scope": "Supported: a black background with one grey 4-connected shape (blob, rectangle or line of 3 to about 20 cells) and 2-4 marker colours by default (up to 8 on request). Markers are isolated single pixels, and the minimum distance is 1, 2 or 3, including diagonal contact with the shape. Grids are 10x10 half the time; otherwise each side is drawn from 7..16 as a synthetic extension, and any side from 5 to 30 may be requested. Explicit shape plus markers reproduces the fixtures. Explicit shape alone gets random markers. Not supported: multiple grey shapes, multi-pixel markers, non-black backgrounds, a shape colour other than 5, and ties in random scenes.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "The shape is 4-connected, grey (5), and strictly larger than any marker (at least 3 cells in random scenes).",
    "Markers use colours from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9} and never touch the shape orthogonally. Diagonal contact is allowed.",
    "Markers never touch each other, even diagonally, so each marker is its own single-pixel object.",
    "In random scenes, every marker at the minimum distance has the target colour, and all other markers are strictly farther away.",
    "Each of the num_colors-1 distractor colours appears at least once, so a distractor is always present.",
    "The output always differs from the input, because the target colour is never 5 and at least one marker is erased.",
    "Explicit-marker ties are resolved by the first nearest marker in row-major order, matching canonical train pair 3."
  ],
